# PDF to Slidev Presentation Workflow

When the user provides a PDF to convert into a new presentation, follow these steps in order.

## 1. Extract text with OCR

Run the existing OCR script against the provided PDF:

```bash
python3 ocr_extract.py "/path/to/file.pdf"
```

Prerequisites (install once if missing): `brew install tesseract tesseract-lang poppler` and `pip3 install pdf2image pytesseract Pillow`.

Read the output carefully — OCR is imperfect. Cross-reference with the original PDF (use the Read tool on the PDF) to fix garbled text, missing code blocks, and broken tables.

## 2. Create the presentation subdirectory

Choose a short, lowercase, English slug (e.g. `introduction`, `lambda-calculus`, `clojure`).

```
<slug>/
  package.json
  slides.md
  global-top.vue   (copy verbatim from any existing deck — see step 3bis)
  public/logos/    (if images are needed)
```

## 3. Create `package.json`

Use this template — only change the `name` and `build --base` path:

```json
{
  "name": "programacion-III-<slug>",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "slidev",
    "build": "slidev build --base /programacion-III/<slug>/",
    "export": "slidev export"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "@slidev/cli": "^52.14.1",
    "@slidev/theme-bricks": "^0.25.0"
  },
  "overrides": {
    "markdown-exit": "1.0.0-beta.9"
  }
}
```

The `overrides` pin is required — see `AGENTS.md`'s "`npm install` on a new deck can pull a broken `markdown-exit`" note. Add it before the first `npm install`, not after hitting the bug.

Then run `npm install` inside the new directory (with `ulimit -n 10240` on macOS).

## 3bis. Copy `global-top.vue`

Every deck needs this file at its root — it renders the fixed home icon (top-right) that links back to the landing page, and is hidden automatically during PDF export/print. It's fully generic (identical byte-for-byte across every deck), so just copy it verbatim from any existing deck, e.g.:

```bash
cp js-contemporaneo/global-top.vue <slug>/global-top.vue
```

Do this before the first local test — a deck missing this file has no way back to the index, and the omission is easy to miss because everything else still builds and runs fine.

## 4. Write `slides.md`

Use `theme: bricks` and follow the conventions from the existing `introduction/slides.md`:

- Frontmatter: theme, title, info, author, keywords, transition, mdc
- Use Slidev layouts: `center`, `default`, `two-cols`, `image-right`, etc.
- Code blocks: use Slidev syntax highlighting with line highlights `{all|1|2-4}`
- Use `<v-click>` for progressive reveal
- Use UnoCSS/Tailwind utility classes for layout (grid, flex, absolute positioning)
- Logos go in `public/logos/` — download from CDN (devicons, simpleicons) or create SVGs
- Language: Spanish (matching the original PDF content)

## 5. Download icons/logos

Use jsdelivr CDN for devicons:

```bash
curl -sL "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/<name>/<name>-original.svg" -o public/logos/<name>.svg
```

Verify each SVG is actual content (not a redirect/HTML page). If broken, create a minimal custom SVG.

## 6. Update root `index.html`

The landing is a filterable card grid (`.grid > .card[data-category]`), not a list — see `AGENTS.md` for the full markup reference. Two cases:

- **The slug already has a placeholder card** (core topics from `PLAN-UNIDAD-4.md` section 5, or one of the four optionals from section 7): find its `<div class="card" data-category="proximamente" data-pending="true">` (or `data-category="extra" data-pending="true"`), remove `data-pending` and the `<span class="badge ...">`, set `data-category="unidad"` if it was a core topic, and add the real `.card-actions` block (`.view-link` pills to `./slug/` and `./slug-docs/` with `data-dev-port`/`data-dev-path`, plus a `.card-download-menu` listing every PDF). Copy the exact structure from an already-activated unit card (e.g. "JS Contemporáneo") as a template.
- **Brand-new topic with no placeholder**: add a new `.card` with `data-category="unidad"` (or `"extra"`) following the same structure, in the correct position — order is always Unidades → Próximamente → Extra → Deprecado.

Also update `dev.sh`'s `MODULES`/`PORTS` arrays (the Slidev deck only — `-docs/` VitePress sites are not started by `dev.sh`, run `npm run docs:dev` from their own folder) and `.gitignore` (copy the 4-line pattern used for every existing `<slug>`/`<slug>-docs` pair).

## 7. Test locally

```bash
cd <slug> && ulimit -n 10240 && npx slidev --port <port>
```

Or from the root: `npm run dev` (uses `dev.sh` which auto-discovers all presentations).

Verify every slide renders correctly. Check for broken images, OCR artifacts, and layout issues.

## 8. Commit and push (optional — only if user requests)

The user always reviews the generated presentation manually before committing. Only commit and push if explicitly asked.
